    "title": "Chipotle hockey jersey deal lets you score a free meal on April 20",
    "text": "Updated April 20, 2026, 1:46 p.m. ETChipotle fans will get to take advantage of a popular promotion from the restaurant chain. It's a buy one, get one deal on entrées just in time for the NHL playoffs.The offer is available to any customer who wears a hockey jersey at participating restaurants in the U.S. and Canada after 3 p.m. local time on Monday, April 20. This is the sixth consecutive year the company has offered this deal.“Our Hockey Jersey BOGO has become a tradition that brings fans together around the Stanley Cup Playoffs and reflects our deep connection to the hockey community,” said Stephanie Perdue, Interim Chief Marketing Officer at Chipotle, in a news release. The chain last year announced that its years-long partnership with the National Hockey League had been extended.The NHL regular season ended on April 16 and the playoffs started on April 18.Chipotle unveils first-ever hockey jersey as part of promotionIn addition to the BOGO deal, Chipotle has unveiled its first-ever limited-edition hockey jersey and is giving Chipotle Rewards Members a chance to score a sweater.Chipotle said only 75 jerseys will be available exclusively through the Chipotle Rewards Exchange. Rewards members will be able to exchange 10 rewards points for an entry to win one jersey. Each Rewards member can enter up to 20 times. This started Saturday, April 18 and will run through Saturday, May 2.The jersey features the number 53, which Chipotle says is a nod to the 53 real ingredients on its core menu. The name on the back reads \"Chipper,\" which the chain says is a term referring to Chipotle that has been popularized by hockey players and fans on social media over the past few years.Gabe Hauari is a national trending news reporter at USA TODAY. You can follow him on X @GabeHauari or email him at Gdhauari@gannett.com.",
